    {
        "content": "<p>So it seems something changed in 4.36.</p>",
        "id": 632599931,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1792259868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK; the number of jobs having doubled is consistent with the numbers. And since Mathlib is building faster with v4.36, it likely is not a sign that it takes longer. But it is a bit  confusing...</p>",
        "id": 632600882,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1792260120
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it happened in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14906\">lean4#14906</a>.</p>",
        "id": 632602064,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1792260456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's mentioned in the <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/releases/v4.36.0/\">release notes</a>, but I agree it's not super clear.</p>",
        "id": 632602189,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1792260490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"315577\">@Mac Malone</span> was this intended? Even if it was it is probably a good idea to mention it somewhere (I mean, mention explicitly that the number doubles).</p>",
        "id": 632602458,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1792260579
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/14906\">#14906</a> splits leanir code generation into a separate Lake job and target . The leanArts facet on modules and libraries id deprecated and replaced with two distinct facets: elabArts and irArts. For backwards compatibility, uses of leanArts delegate to irArts.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>OK. I admit I did not every item of the release notes... (and if I had I would not have understood that it would double the number of build jobs for Mathlib).</p>",
        "id": 632602481,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1792260584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The numbers seem to have gone down again btw</p>",
